message.content:
Below is a **road‑map** you can follow to build a modern, scalable, and maintainable frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and best‑practice pointers.  
Feel free to skip sections that already exist in your project or to adapt the stack to your team’s preferences.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| Step | What to do | Why it matters |
|------|------------|----------------|
| **Define core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, cart, checkout, user account, admin panel, reviews, recommendations, analytics, PWA, SEO, accessibility | Keeps scope focused and lets you pick the right tech |
| **Create wireframes / mockups** | Use Figma/Sketch/Adobe XD | Visualise layout, user flows, and get stakeholder buy‑in early |
| **Choose a design system** | Tailwind CSS + Headless UI, or Material‑UI + ThemeProvider | Consistent UI, faster prototyping |
| **Plan data contracts** | API spec (OpenAPI/GraphQL) | Frontend and backend stay in sync |

---

## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Recommended Tech | Why |
|-------|------------------|-----|
| **Framework** | **React** (Next.js) | SSR/SSG, rich ecosystem, great for e‑commerce |
| **State** | **Redux Toolkit** + **RTK Query** | Predictable state, built‑in async logic |
| **Routing** | **next/router** | File‑based routing, dynamic routes for products |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS** + **clsx** | Utility‑first, easy theming |
| **Component library** | **Headless UI** (or **MUI**) | Accessible primitives |
| **Form handling** | **react-hook-form** | Lightweight, good for validation |
| **API calls** | **axios** or **fetch** (via RTK Query) | Handles auth, retries, caching |
| **Payments** | **Stripe Elements** | PCI‑compliant, easy to integrate |
| **Auth** | **NextAuth.js** | OAuth, JWT, session handling |
| **Testing** | **Jest** + **React Testing Library** | Unit + integration tests |
| **Linting/Formatting** | **ESLint**, **Prettier** | Code quality |
| **CI/CD** | **GitHub Actions** | Automated lint, test, build, deploy |
| **Hosting** | **Vercel** (or Netlify) | Zero‑config, instant preview, CDN |
| **Analytics** | **Google Analytics** + **Sentry** | User behavior + error tracking |
| **PWA** | **next-pwa** | Offline support, add‑to‑home screen |

> **Tip** – If you prefer a SPA, swap Next.js for Create‑React‑App or Vite and keep the same libraries.

---

